    <string name="general_infotitle">General settings info</string>
    <string name="general_infomsg">This section contains settings that provide basic optimization options.\n\nSystem settings: this category offers options that are normally hidden from the user (It\'s recommended to leave default settings).\n\nCPU settings: this category offers options such as efficiency or heat management (It\'s recommended to leave default settings).\n\nGPU settings: this category offers options such as efficiency boost, etc. (It\'s recommended to leave default settings).\n\nMemory settings: this category offers options related to (ZRAM) virtual memory optimizations (It\'s recommended to leave default settings).\n\nStorage settings: this category offers settings to improve UFS energy efficiency (It\'s recommended to leave default settings).\n\nBattery settings: this category offers battery charging protection options, among others.</string>
    <string name="general_battprotectwarningtitle">Important!</string>
    <string name="general_battprotectwarningmsg">Make sure that battery protection on system is disabled to avoid conflicts/issues.\nYou can check this in Settings app &gt; Battery &gt; Battery protection.\n\nYou may need to re-plug the charger for the changes to take effect.</string>
    <string name="general_optimizeappstitle">Apps optimization notice!</string>
    <string name="general_optimizeappsmsg">It\'s recommended to optimize applications every two weeks or after performing major system updates, this helps improve both performance and battery efficiency on device.\n\nNote: device may heat up during optimization and process may take several minutes.</string>
