    <string name="advanced_infotitle">Advanced settings info</string>
    <string name="advanced_infomsg">This section contains advanced options such as frequency options or undervoltage options.\n\nFrequency settings: this section contains frequency-related settings to allows you to control processing speed for little (efficiency) and big (performance) cores (It\'s recommended to leave default settings).\n\nUndervolt settings: this section contains options related to voltage intensity for each device component, these are based on percentage margins, each slider bar offers undervoltage values, such as CPU, GPU, RAM, display, audio, etc. (It\'s recommended to leave default settings).\n\nNote: increasing the frequency/speed will increase the heat generated by the device and these settings may make your device UNSTABLE or cause FREEZES depending on frequency and/or undervoltage settings you are using.</string>
